{"document_id":"cir-beta-glucan-safety-assessment-v1","title":"Beta-Glucan — CIR safety-assessment factual card","source":"Cosmetic Ingredient Review (CIR)","source_family":"CIR","source_url":"https://journals.sagepub.com/doi/10.1177/1091581816651606","published_year":2016,"document_type":"regulatory-safety-provenance-card","evidence_tier":"regulatory-safety-provenance","chunk_text":"Paraphrased CIR conclusion: in the Safety Assessment of Microbial Polysaccharide Gums (2016) the CIR Expert Panel concluded the assessed gums, including Beta-Glucan, are safe in the present practices of use and concentration in cosmetics. Beta-glucan was reported as practically non-irritating to rabbit eyes (weakly irritating in a HET-CAM assay). Paraphrased factual summary; no verbatim CIR text is stored.","source_locator":"Safety Assessment of Microbial Polysaccharide Gums as Used in Cosmetics (CIR, 2016).","citation_text":"Cosmetic Ingredient Review. Safety Assessment of Microbial Polysaccharide Gums as Used in Cosmetics. Int J Toxicol. 2016.","claim_category":"ingredient-regulatory-safety-context","clinical_review_status":"pending: qualified review must reconfirm against source before activation.","reuse_rights_status":"attribution_only","reuse_rights_basis":"Factual paraphrase with attribution and source link; protected expression not reproduced.","verification_status":"verified_paraphrase","verified_by":"web-search-assisted draft — reviewer must reconfirm against source","verified_at":"2026-07-27","product_specific":false,"attribution_required":true,"routine_selection_allowed":false,"ingredient_ids":["beta-glucan"],"ingredient_names":["Beta-Glucan"],"inci_names":["Beta-Glucan"]}
{"document_id":"reg-ectoin-status-v1","title":"Ectoin — regulatory status factual card","source":"Regulatory status summary","source_family":"regulatory-status","source_url":"https://health.ec.europa.eu/scientific-committees/scientific-committee-consumer-safety-sccs/sccs-opinions_en","published_year":"","document_type":"regulatory-safety-provenance-card","evidence_tier":"regulatory-safety-provenance","chunk_text":"Paraphrased regulatory status: no dedicated CIR or EU SCCS cosmetic safety assessment for Ectoin was located; it is used in EU/US cosmetics without a dedicated panel opinion. This card records the absence of a dedicated assessment, not a safety conclusion. Paraphrased factual summary; no verbatim text is stored.","source_locator":"Absence of a dedicated CIR/SCCS cosmetic assessment for Ectoin.","citation_text":"Regulatory status summary for Ectoin in cosmetics (no dedicated CIR/SCCS opinion located).","claim_category":"ingredient-regulatory-safety-context","clinical_review_status":"pending: qualified review must establish an appropriate source before activation.","reuse_rights_status":"attribution_only","reuse_rights_basis":"Factual status paraphrase with attribution; protected expression not reproduced.","verification_status":"verified_status_no_dedicated_assessment","verified_by":"web-search-assisted draft — reviewer to source a dedicated assessment","verified_at":"2026-07-27","product_specific":false,"attribution_required":true,"routine_selection_allowed":false,"ingredient_ids":["ectoin"],"ingredient_names":["Ectoin"],"inci_names":["Ectoin"]}
{"document_id":"reg-retinal-status-v1","title":"Retinal (Retinaldehyde) — SCCS/regulatory status factual card","source":"EU SCCS / regulatory status","source_family":"regulatory-status","source_url":"https://health.ec.europa.eu/system/files/2023-08/sccs_o_261.pdf","published_year":"","document_type":"regulatory-safety-provenance-card","evidence_tier":"regulatory-safety-provenance","chunk_text":"Paraphrased regulatory status: there is no dedicated CIR assessment for Retinal (retinaldehyde). The EU SCCS Vitamin A opinion (SCCS/1639/21) and the EU retinol concentration limits (Regulation 2024/996: ~0.05% body lotion, ~0.3% other leave-on/rinse-off) cover retinol and retinyl esters; retinaldehyde is treated as a distinct category not covered by those retinol restrictions. This card records regulatory context, not a safety conclusion. Paraphrased factual summary; no verbatim text is stored.","source_locator":"EU SCCS Vitamin A opinion (retinol/esters); Regulation 2024/996; retinaldehyde outside those limits.","citation_text":"EU SCCS Opinion on Vitamin A (SCCS/1639/21); Commission Regulation (EU) 2024/996. Retinaldehyde regulatory context.","claim_category":"ingredient-regulatory-safety-context","clinical_review_status":"pending: qualified review must establish an appropriate source before activation.","reuse_rights_status":"attribution_only","reuse_rights_basis":"Factual status paraphrase with attribution; protected expression not reproduced.","verification_status":"verified_status_no_dedicated_assessment","verified_by":"web-search-assisted draft — reviewer to confirm current retinoid rules","verified_at":"2026-07-27","product_specific":false,"attribution_required":true,"routine_selection_allowed":false,"ingredient_ids":["retinal"],"ingredient_names":["Retinal"],"inci_names":["Retinal"]}
{"document_id":"reg-mandelic-acid-status-v1","title":"Mandelic Acid — regulatory status factual card","source":"Regulatory status summary","source_family":"regulatory-status","source_url":"https://www.cir-safety.org/sites/default/files/ahas.pdf","published_year":"","document_type":"regulatory-safety-provenance-card","evidence_tier":"regulatory-safety-provenance","chunk_text":"Paraphrased regulatory status: Mandelic Acid is an alpha hydroxy acid but has no dedicated CIR or SCCS safety assessment (unlike glycolic and lactic acid, which are covered in the CIR AHA report). General AHA guidance applies — CIR recommended a maximum of about 10% AHA in consumer products, and AHAs increase UV sensitivity (sun protection advised). This card records the absence of a dedicated assessment plus general AHA context, not a mandelic-specific conclusion. Paraphrased factual summary; no verbatim text is stored.","source_locator":"No dedicated CIR/SCCS mandelic-acid assessment; general AHA guidance (CIR Alpha Hydroxy Acids report).","citation_text":"Regulatory status summary for Mandelic Acid; general AHA guidance from CIR Safety Assessment of Alpha Hydroxy Acids.","claim_category":"ingredient-regulatory-safety-context","clinical_review_status":"pending: qualified review must establish an appropriate source before activation.","reuse_rights_status":"attribution_only","reuse_rights_basis":"Factual status paraphrase with attribution; protected expression not reproduced.","verification_status":"verified_status_no_dedicated_assessment","verified_by":"web-search-assisted draft — reviewer to source a dedicated assessment","verified_at":"2026-07-27","product_specific":false,"attribution_required":true,"routine_selection_allowed":false,"ingredient_ids":["mandelic-acid"],"ingredient_names":["Mandelic Acid"],"inci_names":["Mandelic Acid"]}
